# The backend image builds from the REPOSITORY ROOT (it carries harness/ and
# scripts/ alongside backend/), so without this file the whole working tree —
# .git, node_modules, local virtualenvs, crawl output — gets shipped to the
# Docker daemon on every build.
#
# Note this does NOT apply to the frontend image: .dockerignore is read from the
# build context root, and that build's context is ./frontend.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Virtualenvs and caches — rebuilt inside the image, and platform-wrong anyway.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/node_modules
**/.next

# Secrets. The image never needs them; compose injects env at run time.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example
**/auth_state.json
**/credentials.json
.skill-backups

# Crawl output and per-site state. The container gets these as named volumes,
# so baking a copy in would both bloat the image and shadow the mount.
harness/workspaces/*
!harness/workspaces/.gitkeep
harness/run-logs
harness/media
backend/agent-workspace

# Not used by the backend image (the frontend has its own build).
frontend

# Docs and media the runtime never reads. demo.gif alone is 5.7MB.
docs
*.md
!README.md
